From 9e1d9e12800044c370327de652ae1084390a06f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:57:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: park the rms_norm pre-add fold - it makes the build
 nondeterministic

Stock b10237 reads one repeated perplexity value across 20 loads of the runner
gate command; the folded build spans 3.9269-3.9448, and about 20% of single
draws land outside the 0.1% gate. Since the runner takes ONE measurement per
arm, that is a ~20% false-rejection rate on any submission, and the excursions
are real wrong numbers rather than measurement noise.

A grouped bisect (10 loads per arm, spread as the statistic) pins it to this
fold alone: disabling it returns 3.9318 ten times out of ten, as do all-off,
norm-off and folds-off, while 0009 and 0036 alone still jitter at 0.186% and
0.379%.

Two mechanisms were proposed and both measured DEAD:
 - the loop-2 global read-back: removed it entirely (values kept in a register
   array, confirmed register-allocated from the fatbin, speed-neutral) and the
   jitter survived at 1/12 outside the gate;
 - buffer aliasing: the disjointness guard in ggml_cuda_rms_norm_pre_add_detect
   already covers dst vs add_dst and a host-side audit saw it hold 3/3 loads,
   while the overlaps that do exist are byte-identical across loads whose
   perplexity differs.

So the defect is real, localised and unidentified. Off by default until it is
understood; GGML_CUDA_PRE_ADD_NORM=1 re-enables it for investigation.

Verified: parked build reads 3.9318 ten times out of ten, exactly the way stock
reads 3.9314 ten times out of ten. Cost pp512 4911.7 -> 4851.9 (-1.22%) and
tg128 164.58 -> 159.94 (-2.82%).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
index 23d73b011..ee7a95e2d 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -6769,8 +6769,17 @@ static void ggml_cuda_graph_evaluate_and_capture(ggml_backend_cuda_context * cud
                                                    std::atoi(getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_ROPE_GROUP"));
             static const bool disable_set_rows_group = getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SET_ROWS_GROUP") != nullptr &&
                                                    std::atoi(getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SET_ROWS_GROUP"));
-            static const bool disable_pre_add_norm = getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_PRE_ADD_NORM") != nullptr &&
-                                                   std::atoi(getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_PRE_ADD_NORM"));
+            // PARKED (round 45).  This fold makes the build nondeterministic at the
+            // runner gate shape: stock reads one repeated value across 20 loads and
+            // the folded build spans 3.9269-3.9448, ~20% of single draws outside the
+            // 0.1% gate.  A grouped bisect pins it to this fold alone; two proposed
+            // mechanisms (the loop-2 global read-back, and dst/add_dst aliasing) were
+            // both implemented or instrumented and both measured DEAD, so the defect
+            // is real but unidentified -- see README rounds 43-45.  Off by default
+            // until it is understood; correctness before 2.98% of decode.
+            // GGML_CUDA_PRE_ADD_NORM=1 re-enables it, for investigation only.
+            static const bool disable_pre_add_norm = !(getenv("GGML_CUDA_PRE_ADD_NORM") != nullptr &&
+                                                       std::atoi(getenv("GGML_CUDA_PRE_ADD_NORM")));
             static const bool disable_norm_quant = getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_NORM_QUANT") != nullptr &&
                                                    std::atoi(getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_NORM_QUANT"));
             static const bool disable_l2_norm_group = getenv("GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_L2_NORM_GROUP") != nullptr &&
